{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_6rhli26bpwiqumf3stmbeqfrrf2agxre554zuh4olxqi5ea2qydq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass (7/7). The implementation translates the C Hamming ECC encoder/decoder to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n- **`log2uint8`**: Uses Rust's `u8::leading_zeros()` to compute floor(log2(v)) — equivalent to C's `31 - __builtin_clz(v)` for 8-bit input.\n- **`hecc_encode`/`hecc_encode_impl`**: Walks the bit positions, skipping powers of 2 (parity slots), accumulating `p1` (XOR of indices for set bits) and `p2` (overall parity), then writes the combined parity byte. Partial blocks zero-pad the input but only emit the actual data bytes plus one parity byte.\n- **`hecc_decode`/`hecc_decode_impl`**: Recomputes `p1`/`p2` over the data, XORs against the stored check byte. If the syndrome is nonzero, uses overall parity to detect double errors (return `None`), and corrects single-bit data errors via the syndrome-to-position formula (`p1 - log2(p1) - 2`).\n- The implementation is fully safe Rust — no `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unwrap`-on-failure paths, no `unimplemented!()` left.\n\nThe `cmp` import was retained from the scaffold (the rule forbids modifying signatures/structs/constants but allows touching bodies; I left the `use std::cmp;` line untouched but it's effectively unused — harmless and within the rules)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":29944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":963,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fcef550-b308-4a7e-8af4-d250021234e2","uuid":"8b0c621d-1fac-4815-a8a4-deff22581eb9"}
